     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, about twice the maximum labeled dose. I don't know of any indication that supports it, and it carries a real risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis. I'd rather not place it than rely on a downstream check to catch it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower dose if you're titrating.\n- **Add a note to the order.** I can include text such as \"titrate per glycemic response\" or \"pharmacy to review.\"\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. The order can then go through the standard override process in the order-entry system. Tell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
